// The collisions, and nothing else. `q` and `v` are the names main.bit's generic
// declarations give their `Option<T>` parameter and its argument; the colliding
// parameter's TYPE is irrelevant (the ticket measured `int`, `string` and a
// class, all reproducing). A LOCAL named `q` here does NOT reproduce, so these
// must stay PARAMETERS — and they must stay in this file, which sorts after
// main.bit, because the winner is whichever declaration the arena sweep reaches
// LAST (a single file reproduces too, when the collision is written below the
// generic; the ticket's "one file compiles" row was an artifact of order).
fn other(q: int): int {
  return q + 1
}

fn twice(v: int): int {
  return v * 2
}
